,"category":"911 Models","description":"The #11 Porsche 936/81 (936-003) started the 1981 Le Mans from pole position and won the race driven by Jacky Ickx and Derek Bell. All the factory built 936 had now won Le Mans: chassis 002 in 1976, 001 in 1977 and 003 in 1981.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/HDK-2072-bdff4ba7.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Porsche-936_81-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-936-81/","specs":{"Layout":"Mid-engine / flat-6","Engine":"flat-6","Displacement":"2,650 cc","Power":"629 cv","Torque":"540 Nm","Top speed":"359 km/h","0–100 km/h":null,"Production":"5"}}},{"id":"X911.SC..San.Reno.","x":1981,"y":4.045,"name":"911 SC “San Reno”","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 SC “San Reno”","year":1981,"category":"911 Models","description":"Röhrl's one-off drive at the 1981 San Remo Rally is regarded as one of the greatest drives ever","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/walter-rohrl-1981-porsche-911sc-san-remo-1.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/walter-rohrl-1981-porsche-911sc-san-remo-1.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-911-sc-san-reno/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"X924.Carrera.GTP","x":1981,"y":3,"name":"924 Carrera GTP","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"924 Carrera GTP","year":1981,"category":"Misc Models","description":"Porsche brought a handful of 924 Carrera GTs to compete in the GTP class in the 1980 Le Mans 24 hour race, with the best car finishing sixth overall. Further development of the Carrera GT platform led to even more homologation specials, culminating in 1981 with the wild 924 Carrera GTR. Ferociously quick, the 924