"custom":{"model":"911 Cabriolet","year":1994,"category":"911 Models","description":"The 993 initially launched with two models: the rear-wheel-drive Carrera and all-wheel-drive Carrera 4 in both coupe and cabriolet body styles. The M64/01 3.6-liter 964 engine layout was retained but refined. The crankshaft vibration dampener was eliminated in the 993. Hydraulic valve lifters were utilized for the first time in a 911 engine, valve weight was reduced, plus the 993 exhaust system was completely redesigned. When the 993’s M64/05 engine went into production it was rated at 272 horsepower at 6,100 rpm and 243 pound-feet of torque at 5,000 rpm. Also, Porsche changed the G50 manual transmission and added a sixth gear; this gave the normally aspirated (NA) 993 a top speed of 168 miles per hour.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Porsche-993-buyers-guide-1995_Porsche_911CarreraCabriolet-0-1024-art-scale-2_00x-1-e1700157527836.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Porsche-911-Carrera-Cabriolet-993-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-911-cabriolet-1994-1997/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / flat-6","Engine":"flat-6","Displacement":"3,600 cc","Power":"272 cv","Torque":"329 Nm","Top speed":"275 km/h","0–100 km/h":"5.6 s","Production":"15,499"}}},{"id":"X911.Carrera.2","x":1994,"y":3.955,"name":"911 Carrera","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 Carrera","year":1994,"category":"911 Models","description":"Introduced in late 1994 the standard 911 Carrera of the 993 generation was fitted with a development of the M64 3.6-liter flat six that had been found in the prior 964 generation. With a redesigned exhaust system and new hydraulic lifters, the engine produced 272 horsepower. For the 1996 model year, a Targa variant was introduced, and a variable intake runner system (called VarioRam) was added to the entire Carrera lineup, bumping horsepower to 285. Approximately 23,000 coupes were built, 15,500 cabriolets, and 4,500 Targa’s, in both manual and automatic (Tiptronic) transmission. Overlapping with the last year of production, it was replaced by the 911 Carrera of the 996 generation for model year 1998. This post focuses on the base coupe version.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/1994_Porsche_911Carrera-0-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Porsche-911-Carrera-Coupe-993-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-911-carrera-1994-1997/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / flat-6","Engine":"flat-6","Displacement":"3,600 cc","Power":"272 cv","Torque":"329 Nm","Top speed":"275 km/h","0–100 km/h":"5.6 s","Production":"23,127"}}},{"id":"X911.Cup.3.8","x":1994,"y":4.045,"name":"911 Cup 3.8","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 Cup 3.8","year":1994,"category":"911 Models","description":"Developed at Porsche’s race department using the platform of their new 993 Carrera 2","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/Porsche-911-Cup-3.8-993-1994-1998.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Porsche-911-Cup-3.8-993-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-911-cup-3-8-993-1994-1998/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / flat-6","Engine":"flat-6","Displacement":"3,600 cc","Power":"314 cv","Torque":null,"Top speed":"280 km/h","0–100 km/h":null,"Production":"195"}}},{"id":"X911.Turbo.3.6.S","x":1994,"y":4.135,"name":"911 Turbo 3.6 S","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 Turbo 3.6 S","year":1994,"category":"911 Models","description":"'36S' package included body kit and mighty X88 'S' motor. 19 non 'slant nose' or Package cars were made for USA.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Screenshot-2019-10-22-17.01.50.png","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads