":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Cayenne.Cabriolet.Concept.Car","x":2002,"y":2.955,"name":"Cayenne Cabriolet Concept Car","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Cayenne Cabriolet Concept Car","year":2002,"category":"Misc Models","description":"It is not clear if the Cayenne Cabriolet was ever intended for production, but considering how much work was put into the concept car, the project was taken seriously. The car has the nose and brakes from the Cayenne Turbo, but this concept car might have a normally aspirated engine, if at all. Porsche has not unveiled any technical information.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/stuttcars-cayenne-cabrio-concept-01-copyright-porsche.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/stuttcars-cayenne-cabrio-concept-01-copyright-porsche.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-cayenne-cabriolet-concept-car-2002/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Cayenne.S","x":2002,"y":3.045,"name":"Cayenne S","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Cayenne S","year":2002,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The first-generation Cayenne saw the introduction of the Cayenne S in 2002. While the base Cayenne had a 3.2-L VR6 engine, the Cayenne S got a 4.5 L V8 with more power and torque. The extremely short and compact normal-aspirated V8 produced 340 hp and 310 lb⋅ft of torque. Acceleration for the Cayenne S is strong for an SUV, with 0–60 mph taking 6.9 seconds and the top speed being 150 mph. The Cayenne S also have some visual changes to better identify it, but was otherwise standard Cayenne fair.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Porsche-Cayenne-S-955.png","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Porsche-Cayenne-S-955.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-cayenne-s-2002-2007/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Cayenne.Turbo","x":2002,"y":3.135,"name":"Cayenne Turbo","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Cayenne Turbo","year":2002,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The first-generation Cayenne Turbo 955 has 450 PS (331 kW), and can accelerate from 0–100 km/h (62 mph) in 5.3 seconds. Under the hood, the Cayenne Turbo was fitted with a turbocharged 4.5-liter V8 unit mated to a standard 6-speed automatic. Thanks to the standard air-suspension, the Turbo version could get up to 28 cm (11”) of ground clearance. It was inconceivable for a Porsche fan to accept an SUV from the famous sports-car manufacturer. But the car was needed. The German brand needed a car to sell in volumes and save them from a foreseeable financial collapse. The Cayenne Turbo managed to satisfy the customers who were looking for a performance vehicle in an SUV shape.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Porsche-Cayenne-Turbo-2002-2007.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Porsche-Cayenne-Turbo-2002-2007.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-cayenne-turbo-2002-2007/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Boxster.1","x":2003,"y":1.955,"name":"Boxster","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Boxster","year":2003,"category":"Boxster & Cayman Models","description":"A mild facelift for the first generation Porsche Boxster","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Boxster-986-2855_22.jpeg","toolti