Cabriolet","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 Turbo Cabriolet","year":2008,"category":"911 Models","description":"The 20-year tradition within the 911 Series of the 911 Turbo with a classic soft top is continued with this open top model. Firstly, the open 2+2 seater offers the driving performance of a high-performance sports car while still providing convertible driving pleasure. Secondly, compared to the competition the 911 Turbo Cabriolet is economical in its fuel consumption, thanks to its deliberate design, outstanding aerodynamics and advanced engine technology","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/PORSCHE-911-Turbo-Cabriolet-997-2906_22.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/Porsche-911-Turbo-Cabriolet-997-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-911-turbo-cabriolet-997-2008-2009/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / flat-6","Engine":"flat-6","Displacement":"3,600 cc","Power":"480 cv","Torque":"624 Nm","Top speed":"311 km/h","0–100 km/h":"3.7 s","Production":"6,099"}}},{"id":"X911.GT2.2","x":2008,"y":4.09,"name":"911 GT2","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 GT2","year":2008,"category":"911 Models","description":"It was the most powerful and fastest roadgoing 911 Porsche ever created","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/PORSCHE-911-GT2-997-2910_19.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/Porsche-911-GT2-997-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-911-gt2-997-2008-2009/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / flat-6","Engine":"flat-6","Displacement":"3,600 cc","Power":"530 cv","Torque":"700 Nm","Top speed":"328 km/h","0–100 km/h":"3.5 s","Production":"1,242"}}},{"id":"Boxster.Limited.Edition","x":2008,"y":2,"name":"Boxster Limited Edition","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Boxster Limited Edition","year":2008,"category":"Boxster & Cayman Models","description":"Porsche unveiled its 2008 Limited Edition Boxster and Boxster S models at a private gathering at the occasion of the 2007 New York Auto Show. Largely inspired by the 2007 911 GT3 RS, only 250 examples of each model were produced in brilliant orange. Other special exterior features included glossy black painted mirrors, alloy wheels, front and side air inlets, and model designation. The SportDesign package was included as standard which includes aggressive front splitters, a revised rear two-stage spoiler that extends automatically at speed, and an integrated rear diffuser. A sports exhaust system with a dual chromed exhaust tip completed the exterior modifications. On the interior, a numbered ‘Limited Edition’ plaque is found on the glove box door, while the seat inserts, 911 GT3-spec steering wheel, and handbrake lever all receive Alcantara trim, a suede-like material. Orange roll-over hoops, door lever surrounds, shift knob, cup-holder cover trim and even the font on the gear shift pattern carrying bright orange that match the exterior colour and offset the otherwise black interior","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Porsche-Boxster-.png","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Porsche-Boxster-.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-boxster-limited-edition-2008/","specs":{"Layout":"Mid-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Boxster.S.Design.Edition.2","x":2008,"y":2.09,"name":"Boxster S Design Edition 2","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Boxster S Design Edition 2","year":2008,"category":"Boxster & Cayman Models","description":"Along with the Cayman S Sport Porsche gave us a Boxster special in 2008. It was a limited production version of the Boxster S called “Porsche Design Edition 2”. Equipped with the same 303 bhp 3.4-liter boxer engine as the Cayman S Sport, the Boxster S Design Edition 2 stands out thanks to the “Carrara White” colour that’s combined with grey stripes. The 19-inch SportDesign alloys, the side air intakes, the centre console and the dials on the three round instruments are also finished in white. The white theme is complemented by the grey roof and the black leather interior.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/2008-8473-boxster-s-porsche-design-edition-21.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/2008-8473-boxster-s-porsche-design-edition-21.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-boxster-s-design-edition-2-2008/","specs":{"Layout":"Mid-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Boxster.S.Limited.Edition","x":2008,"y":2.18,"name":"Boxster S Limited Edition","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Boxster S Limited Edition","year":2008,"category":"Boxster & Cayman Models","description":"Porsche gave us something special in 2008, the Limited Edition Boxster and Boxster S. Pricing started at $59,900 for the Boxster S version. The Limited Edition’s bright orange paint was previously featured on the race-ready Porsche 911 GT3 RS. The Limited Edition is equipped with a sport exhaust system, and safety bars (also painted orange). The SportDesign package includes “spoiler lips” in the front, an automatically extending and redesigned rear spoiler, and modified rear diffuser. There are black alloy wheels—18-inch on the Boxster and 19-inch on the Boxster S—and black exterior side mirrors, and black front and side air inlets. Black carries over to the seats, carpet, dash, door panels and other surrounding soft surfaces.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/IMG_5695-tiny-2048x0-0.5x0.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/IMG_5695-tiny-2048x0-0.5x0.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-boxster-s-limited-edition-2008/","specs":{"Layout":"Mid-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Cayenne.1","x":2008,"y":2.775,"name":"Cayenne","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Cayenne","year":2008,"category":"Misc Models","description":"On the brinks of the global recession in 2007, Porsche launched the 2008 Cayenne model. Although some addressed it as the second generation, it was more of a refresh, with better technologies and interior.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Cayenne-957-2870_24.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Cayenne-957-2870_24.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-cayenne-2007-2009/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Cayenne.Diesel","x":2008,"y":2.865,"name":"Cayenne Diesel","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Cayenne Diesel","year":2008,"category":"Misc Models","description":"It was the first oil-burner Porsche in history. The European market asked for a diesel engine and the car-maker had to deliver it to keep the sale up in a struggled market affected by the world financial crisis.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Cayenne-Diesel-957-3818_11.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Cayenne-Diesel-957-3818_11.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-cayenne-diesel-2008-2010/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Archi