T3 R Hybrid 2.0 is V2 of its GT3 R Hybrid race car. It’s the second iteration of Porsche’s ground-breaking 911 endurance racer fitted with a Kinetic Energy Recovery System, or KERS. The first version of the 911 GT3 R Hybrid, revealed in 2010, led the 24 Hours of Nurburgring in its first competition run, until a mechanical failure forced it to retire just a few hours before the checkered flag. That failure, irony would have it was due to an issue with the combustion engine, not any of the hybrid components. In October, the car finished the Petit Le Mans at Road Atlanta, part of the American Le Mans Series, where it won its special experimental class…of one car. That weekend, Porsche’s Dr. Daniel Armbruster, who led the hybrid racer’s development team, indicated that further development would focus on integrating the mechanical systems, to cut the weight to that of a standard 911 GT3 RSR, and refining the software.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/Porsche-911-GT3-R-Hybrid-2.0-2011.png","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/Porsche-911-GT3-R-Hybrid-4.0-997-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-911-gt3-r-hybrid-2-0-2011/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / flat-6","Engine":"flat-6","Displacement":"4,000 cc","Power":"679 cv","Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":"2.6 s","Production":null}}},{"id":"X918.RSR.Hybrid.Concept","x":2011,"y":1,"name":"918 RSR Hybrid Concept","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"918 RSR Hybrid Concept","year":2011,"category":"Supercars","description":"The 918 RSR ‘Racing Lab’ is part of a new initiative called Porsche Intelligent Performance","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/car_photo_415909.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/Porsche-918-RSR-Profile-Large-500x373.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-918-rsr-hybrid-concept/","specs":{"Layout":"Mid-engine / V8","Engine":"V8","Displacement":null,"Power":"778 cv","Torque":null,"Top speed":"320 km/h","0–100 km/h":"3.3 s","Production":null}}},{"id":"Cayenne.2","x":2011,"y":2.64,"name":"Cayenne","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Cayenne","year":2011,"category":"Misc Models","description":"With the second generation of the Cayenne, Porsche proved itself very profitable, even though it was hit hard by the world economic crisis from the 2008-2010 period. But the luxury car market didn’t drop the same as the other car-segments. So, the Cayenne went on with a new generation that gathered immediate attention.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Cayenne-4253_16.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Cayenne-4253_16.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-cayenne-2011-2014/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Cayenne.Diesel.1","x":2011,"y":2.73,"name":"Cayenne Diesel","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Cayenne Diesel","year":2011,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The V6 diesel engine was the same unit found in the other Volkswagen group models. The 3.0-liter unit offered 240 hp. It was mated as standard with an 8-speed automatic gearbox. Cayenne Diesel Turbo 3.0 176 kW for 2011 model year. In 2012, power increased to 180 kW. 2013 saw the launch of the Cayenne Diesel S Turbo 4.1 281 kW version.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Cayenne-Diesel-4254_26.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Cayenne-Diesel-4254_26.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-cayenne-diesel-2011-2014/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed",