1-H (Le Mans Prototype Class 1, Hybrid) race car featured a hybrid system that consisted of a turbocharged 2.0V4 petrol engine at the rear axle and an electric motor at the front axle. The electric motor/generator unit (MGU) collected the energy from the front axle under braking and the AER exhaust energy recovery system operated on the exhaust gas – a separate turbocharger ran an alternator. The 2-litre engine sounds like a very small one, but the air flow into the engine was not restricted and up to 4 bar/58 PSI turbo boost pressure was allowed. By the new rules, the instant fuel consumption was limited and therefore the 2-litre engine was the effective choice. The Energy Recovery System (ERS) stored the energy in a battery until the driver activated the electric motor on the front axle.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2014_Porsche_919Hybrid-3-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/2014-Porsche-919-Hybrid-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-919-hybrid-2014/","specs":{"Layout":"Mid-engine / 2.0 L Turbo V4 Hybrid","Engine":"2.0 L Turbo V4 Hybrid","Displacement":"2,000 cc","Power":"760 cv","Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":"2"}}},{"id":"X911.50th.Anniversary.Edition.Turbo.S.Coupe","x":2014,"y":4.405,"name":"911 50th Anniversary Edition Turbo S Coupe","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 50th Anniversary Edition Turbo S Coupe","year":2014,"category":"911 Models","description":"Jerry Seinfeld’s \"1 of 1\" 911 demands top dollar","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Porsche-Seinfeld-911-12.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Porsche-Seinfeld-911-12.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/2014-porsche-911-50th-anniversary-edition-turbo-s-coupe/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.1","x":2014,"y":2.57,"name":"Panamera","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The Panamera received a fairly substantial mid-cycle update for 2014. The base engine, installed in the Panamera version, was an upgraded version of the previously used 3.6-liter V6. For the 2014 model year, it was mated exclusively with a 7-speed (PDK – dual-clutch) automatic gearbox and the 6-speed manual was dropped. It also gained some extra horses. The power of the V6 engine in the Panamera increased ten hp (eight kW) to 306 bhp @ 6200 rpm and 295 ft lbs @ 3750 rpm of torque, while the fuel consumption decreased 0.9 litres to significantly less than nine litres per 100 km.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-970-5783_3.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-970-5783_3.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.4.1","x":2014,"y":2.641666666666667,"name":"Panamera 4","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera 4","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The Panamera received a fairly substantial mid-cycle update for 2014. The base engine, installed in the Panamera 4 version, was an upgraded version of the previously used 3.6-liter V6. For the 2014 model year, it was mated exclusively with a 7-speed (PDK – dual-clutch) automatic gearbox and the 6-speed manual was dropped. It also gained some extra horses. The power of the V6 engine in the Panamera and Panamera 4, for example, increased ten hp (eight kW) to 306 bhp @ 6200 rpm and 295 ft lbs @ 3750 rpm of torque, while the fuel consumption decreased 0.9 litres to significantly less than nine litres per 100 km.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-4-970-5784_5.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-4-970-5784_5.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-4-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.4S.1","x":2014,"y":2.713333333333333,"name":"Panamera 4S","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera 4S","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"Boosting of performance and efficiency is a core competency at Porsche. In developing the new Panamera, this led to an entirely new engine based on the downsizing concept: a V6 engine with three litres displacement and biturbo charging. The V6 biturbo replaces the previous 4.8-litre V8 engine in the Panamera S and Panamera 4S, and it is also used in the new Executive version of the Panamera 4S. Its basic parameters themselves are indicators of progress: 20 hp more power and 20 Newton metres more torque, but up to 18 per cent better fuel economy compared to the V8 engine in the previous model. This not only gives the driver a more powerful and efficient engine; turbocharging results in a maximum torque of 520 Newton metres being available over a very broad range of engine speeds for a superior and uniform power curve, even at low revs.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_Panamera4S-1-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_Panamera4S-1-1024.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-4s-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.4S.Executive","x":2014,"y":2.785,"name":"Panamera 4S Executive","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera 4S Executive","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"As part of the mid-cycle Panamera refresh, Porsche introduced two “Executive” models. The Panamera 4S Executive and the Panamera Turbo Executive. These variants had especially high standards for space, ambience and ride comfort. The wheelbase and passenger compartment were extended by 15 centimetres, and both of these dimensions directly benefit comfort in the rear seating area, since the body was extended behind the B pillar in the long version. For one, this means larger doors for more comfortable entry, and for another even more leg room in front of the two rear bucket seats.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/002-2014-porsche-panamera-executive-qs.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/002-2014-porsche-panamera-executive-qs.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-4s-executive-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.Diesel.1","x":2014,"y":2.856666666666666,"name":"Panamera Diesel","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera Diesel","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The diesel version had to wait until September to be unveiled at the Frankfurt Motor Show and that made sense since Europe was the biggest market for the Panamera diesel. Apart from the visual differences, there were some technological evolutions as well.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-Diesel-4998_2.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-Diesel-4998_2.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-diesel-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.GTS.1","x":2014,"y":2.928333333333333,"name":"Panamera GTS","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera GTS","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"More power and upgraded brakes, a body lowered by ten millimetres and the especially sportily tuned chassis with air suspension and PASM are the major technical modifications that make it the Panamera model capable of cutting it on the racing circuit – without sacrificing practicality.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraGTS-0-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraGTS-0-1024.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-gts-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.S.1","x":2014,"y":3,"name":"Panamera S","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera S","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"A major improvement for the Panamera S was the standard bi-xenon headlights and the option for full LED lamps. The daytime running lights were fitted with light-emitting diodes as standard. The revised front and rear bumpers brought a more aggressive look for the car. The bigger side-scoops in the apron were inspired by those installed on the 911 range. A wider rear windscreen was installed on the new tailgate.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-S-970-5785_5.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-S-970-5785_5.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-s-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.S.E.Hybrid","x":2014,"y":3.071666666666667,"name":"Panamera S E-Hybrid","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera S E-Hybrid","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"In the second generation of the Gran Turismo, Porsche is introducing the world’s first plug-in hybrid to the luxury class. Along with the Panamera S E-Hybrid with 416 hp of system power, two luxurious Executive versions are also making their debut with an extended wheelbase and an entirely new three-litre V6 engine with biturbo charging for the Panamera S and Panamera 4S. An already unrivaled broad base of models has now been extended and consists of ten models offering an even further broader range between sportiness and comfort. New and further developed technologies have enabled fuel savings of up to 56 per cent, while further enhancing operating and driving comfort. The new Panamera underscores its exceptional positioning with an even more expressive design language in the style of the new sports car generations that are marked by tighter lines, more pronounced contours and newly shaped body elements. In short: The Porsche Panamera is even more efficient, sporty, comfortable and elegant. The new generation Gran Turismo celebrates its world premiere at Auto China in Shanghai, which opens its gates on the 21st of April 2013.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraSEHybrid-0-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraSEHybrid-0-1024.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-s-e-hybrid-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.Sport.Turismo","x":2014,"y":3.143333333333334,"name":"Panamera Sport Turismo","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera Sport Turismo","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"Premiere: 2012 September 26, Paris motor show","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2012_Porsche_PanameraSportTurismo-0-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2012_Porsche_PanameraSportTurismo-0-1024.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-sport-turismo-2012/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.Turbo.1","x":2014,"y":3.215,"name":"Panamera Turbo","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera Turbo","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The Porsche Panamera Turbo got an update at the same time as the rest of the Panamera lineup for the 2014 model year. The Panamera facelift was unveiled at the Shanghai Motor Show in 2013 while the Turbo version was introduced in January 2014.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraTurbo-0-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraTurbo-0-1024.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-turbo-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.Turbo.Executive","x":2014,"y":3.286666666666667,"name":"Panamera Turbo Executive","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera Turbo Executive","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The big news for 2014 was the introduction of an all-new Panamera Turbo executive model. It featured a 15 cm (5.9”) longer wheelbase than the Turbo. It was built to offer more legroom in the back. Strangely though, it was built especially for the Chinese market, where the long-wheelbase version of a car, any car, was considered an executive car by default.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraTurboExecutive-3-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraTurboExecutive-3-1024.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-turbo-executive-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.Turbo.S.1","x":2014,"y":3.358333333333333,"name":"Panamera Turbo S","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera Turbo S","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"Porsche is placing its fastest, most powerful and most luxurious Panamera at the peak of its Gran Turismo series: With a power output of 570 bhp and a top speed of 310 km/h plus a particularly extensive and top-quality range of features, the Panamera Turbo S is guaranteed a special status in its market segment. For the first time ever, an Executive version of the Panamera Turbo S is also available with a wheelbase that has been extended by 15 centimetres. As a result, the Panamera Turbo S Executive offers significantly more space and even more comfort, particularly at the rear. Thermal and noise-insulated windows, which include privacy glazing, the interior lighting package designed especially for the rear and a large centre console at the rear are just some of the extensive equipment options that belong to this series. The new top model in the Panamera model line will be celebrating its world premiere at the Tokyo Motor Show.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraTurboS-0-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraTurboS-0-1024.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-turbo-s-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.Turbo.S.Executive","x":2014,"y":3.43,"name":"Panamera Turbo S Executive","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera Turbo S Executive","year":2014,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The advantages offered by the PDCC in terms of driving dynamics are enhanced still further by the Porsche Torque Vectoring Plus system and the electronically controlled rear-axle differential lock with variable locking effect. The system optimises steering behaviour and traction for a sporty driving experience. The Panamera Turbo S comes with the PCCB as standard. These super powerful, race-tested ceramic brakes with yellow brake callipers offer clear advantages over conventional grey cast iron brake discs. A reduction in mass of approx. 50%, a faster handling response and the corrosion resistance of the brake calliper rings guarantee maximum performance.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraTurboSExecutive-0-1024.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/2013_Porsche_PanameraTurboSExecutive-0-1024.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-turbo-s-executive-2014-2016/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displ