a-Turbo-S-E-Hybrid-Executive.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Porsche-Panamera-Turbo-S-E-Hybrid-Executive-500x281.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-turbo-s-e-hybrid-executive-2021-present/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / V8","Engine":"V8","Displacement":null,"Power":"700 cv","Torque":"869 Nm","Top speed":"315 km/h","0–100 km/h":"3.2 s","Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.Turbo.S.E.Hybrid.Sport.Turismo.1","x":2021,"y":3.334444444444444,"name":"Panamera Turbo S E-Hybrid Sport Turismo","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera Turbo S E-Hybrid Sport Turismo","year":2021,"category":"Misc Models","description":"The Panamera Turbo S E-Hybrid Sport Turismo is extreme indulgence at its peak. A family wagon with almost 700 hp on tap and the ability to launch hard enough to strain your back muscles. Porsche claims the car can hit 60 mph in just 3 seconds. It’s impressive on its own, but even then, it seems the carmaker was being conservative as some motoring journalists were able to clock a time of 2.7 seconds. That’s faster than a Ferrari 488 GTB!","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Panamera-Turbo-S-E-Hybrid-Sport-Turismo.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PORSCHE-Panamera-Turbo-S-E-Hybrid-Sport-Turismo-6131_7-500x281.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-panamera-turbo-s-e-hybrid-sport-turismo-2021-present/","specs":{"Layout":"Front-engine / V8","Engine":"V8","Displacement":null,"Power":"700 cv","Torque":"869 Nm","Top speed":"315 km/h","0–100 km/h":"3.1 s","Production":null}}},{"id":"X911.GT2.RS.Clubsport.25","x":2021,"y":4.315,"name":"911 GT2 RS Clubsport 25","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 GT2 RS Clubsport 25","year":2021,"category":"911 Models","description":"A super rare track-only car built to celebrate the 25th anniversary of Manthey-Racing GmbH","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/2021_PORSCHE_991GT2RSmr_FOTO_03_small.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/Porsche-911-GT2-RS-Clubsport-25-991.2-Profile-Large-500x375.png","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-911-gt2-rs-clubsport-25-2021/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / flat-6","Engine":"flat-6","Displacement":"3,800 cc","Power":"701 cv","Torque":"750 Nm","Top speed":"340 km/h","0–100 km/h":"2.8 s","Production":"30"}}},{"id":"X911.Turbo.S.Collaboration.With.Embraer","x":2021,"y":4.405,"name":"911 Turbo S Collaboration With Embraer","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"911 Turbo S Collaboration With Embraer","year":2021,"category":"911 Models","description":"Porsche Exclusive Manufaktur has worked with Brazilian aircraft builder Embraer for a limited-run of private jet-inspired 911 Turbo S cars, according to EVO. The special division is known for its astonishing creations, and this one is perhaps it’s most impressive. The collaboration will yield just 10 cars worldwide. They will be available for purchase by all buyers of the Embraer Phenom 300E business jet, which runs just under £8m. There has been no pricing information discussed for the car, but as you can imagine, the price for the target buyers likely isn’t a concern. The paint scheme for these cars matches the jet. The car combines gloss and satin-gloss finishes for the first time ever on an official 911 build. There are also blue pinstripes designed to match the aircraft. The wheels on these 911 Turbo S models are dark silver with the same blue accents. There’s a unique logo that references the aircraft. It’s on the exterior and the interior of the car. The car also gets each jet’s registration number on the underside of the 911’s active rear wing, which is painted in Speed blue. The engine for this car is the same as the regular 911 Turbo S, which is a 3.8-liter twin-turbocharged flat-six that puts out 641 hp and 590 lb-ft of torque. It has the ability to rocket the car from 0 to 62 mph in 2.7 seconds and all the way to a 205 mph top speed. Inside there’s plenty of blue that features in small quantities on the exterior of the car. There’s also plenty of black and chalk leather upholstery used throughout the car. It’s designed to match the cockpit of the jet. The key for the car is also painted in Speed blue and will feature the registration number of the corresponding jet. The car also comes with a special cover and a’1919 UC Globetimer Embraer’ watch.","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/img_5.jpg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/img_5.jpg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-unveils-911-turbo-s-collaboration-with-embraer/","specs":{"Layout":"Rear-engine / Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Mission.R.Electric","x":2021,"y":0,"name":"Mission R Electric","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Mission R Electric","year":2021,"category":"Concept Cars","description":"A 1073 bhp electric racing concept","image":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/300821-Porsche23879_LDN.jpeg","tooltipImage":"https://www.stuttcars.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/300821-Porsche23879_LDN.jpeg","url":"https://www.stuttcars.com/porsche-mission-r-electric/","specs":{"Layout":"Architecture not listed","Engine":"Architecture not listed","Displacement":null,"Power":null,"Torque":null,"Top speed":null,"0–100 km/h":null,"Production":null}}},{"id":"Panamera.3","x":2021,"y":3.366296296296296,"name":"Panamera","color":"rgba(64,66,66,0.52)","selected":false,"custom":{"model":"Panamera","year":2021,"category":"Misc Models","description":"For the 2021 model year, the Panamera featured a redesigned front fascia, with a different bumper and lower apron. The previously optiona